      "writtenOn": "2026-05-24T10:46:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe instead of adding this `staged_feaddr` and the logic for it (and `staged_perfintraddr` and even more logic in the next patch), we\u0027d better just add a hypercall for the host\u0027s `dmar_msi_write()` instead?\n\nThat might make the code more readable even independently of APIC ID validation: no more tricky `fallthrough`s etc here, just one hypercall with clean semantics for setting all 3 regs DATA, ADDR and UADDR at once, for either FE or PERFINTR (and also reusable for PE in the future, if we support PRQ in the future)?",
      "revId": "e03b1db49315e09f88dabba57796254ef97483c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7aa46804_055c5fb8",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 564,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-26T12:26:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Basically, I\u0027m fine with keeping this staged_feaddr + staged_perfintraddr solution (it seems correct too, after all), so please feel free to resolve this comment.\n\nI\u0027m just thinking that _maybe_ a hypercall would be better, at least because it would avoid this assumption that the host always sets UADDR immediately after ADDR, as well as avoid carrying this extra staged_feaddr + staged_perfintraddr state in pKVM\u0027s data structures.",
      "parentUuid": "53089653_9c90e800",
      "revId": "e03b1db49315e09f88dabba57796254ef97483c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1fdcb7b_de26e3c7",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/pkvm/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 564,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-26T12:50:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "BTW regarding:\n\n\u003e That might make the code more readable even independently of APIC ID validation: no more tricky fallthroughs etc here, just one hypercall with clean semantics for setting all 3 regs DATA, ADDR and UADDR at once, for either FE or PERFINTR (and also reusable for PE in the future, if we support PRQ in the future)?\n\nSo alternatively we could keep this \"staged\" model (if we prefer it over introducing a hypercall), but still, independently of that, refactor the code here, to move handling these dmar_msi_write()-related register writes (FE/PERFINTR ADDR/UADDR/DATA/CTL) into a separate clean function, instead of having all this logic right here as a part of this big `switch`?\n\n(But again, I\u0027m fine with _not_ doing that now.)",
      "parentUuid": "7aa46804_055c5fb8",
      "revId": "e03b1db49315e09f88dabba57796254ef97483c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
